IHAMAICS - licence status
=========================

Short version: this repository cannot be placed under a single open
source licence, because most of what is in it derives from software
that nobody involved in this project owns. Nothing here grants you
rights over the original SAM. Use it at your own risk.

Per-component attribution, including the full text of the licences
that do apply, is in NOTICE.md.

This file is a statement of the project's position, written by its
maintainers. It is not legal advice.


1. The SAM engine, and everything derived from it
-------------------------------------------------

SAM (Software Automatic Mouth) was published in 1982 by Don't Ask
Software, written by Mark Barton. Copyright in it is held by
SoftVoice, Inc. (www.text2speech.com).

Attempts to contact the company have failed and its website was last
updated in 2009, so the status of the original software is best
described as abandonware:

    http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abandonware

The engine in this repository is a reverse-engineered reimplementation
of that software. That covers:

  - the JavaScript port in src/, test/ and dist/
  - the Python port in nvda-addon/synthDrivers/sam/
  - the C renderer in native/
  - the reference audio in native/tests/golden/

Neither this project nor its maintainers hold copyright in SAM, and
neither purports to license it to anyone. No open source licence can
honestly be granted over this code while that remains the case, and
this file does not attempt to grant one.


2. The CMU Pronouncing Dictionary
----------------------------------

nvda-addon/synthDrivers/sam/cmudict.txt is redistributed from
cmusphinx/cmudict under a BSD-2-Clause licence held by Carnegie
Mellon University. That licence requires the copyright notice to be
retained in redistributions, and deems the dictionary file itself to
be source code, so the notice is kept verbatim in the file's own ;;;
header and travels with it into the built add-on.

The full text is in NOTICE.md.


3. Prior work this builds on
-----------------------------

The JavaScript port is by Christian Schiffler (discordier/sam), based
on the C adaptation by Stefan Macke (s-macke/SAM), with refactorings
by Vidar Hokstad and 8BitPimp. The Python and C engines here were
ported from that JavaScript. The constraint in section 1 applies to
all of it.


4. Original work in this repository
------------------------------------

Some material here is not a derivative of SAM: the NVDA driver
integration, the packaging and validation scripts, the build and
differential-testing tooling under native/tools/, and the
documentation.

To the extent that this material can be separated from the engine, the
maintainers place no additional restrictions on its use beyond those
already imposed by sections 1 to 3. This is a waiver of the
maintainers' own claims. It is not, and cannot be, permission to use
SAM itself.


5. What this means in practice
-------------------------------

  - You may read, build, modify and run this code.
  - You may not rely on this project for permission to redistribute
    SAM commercially, or for any assurance about SoftVoice's rights.
  - If you redistribute the add-on, keep NOTICE.md and the cmudict
    header intact; CMU's licence requires it.
  - If SoftVoice, Inc. or a successor in interest objects to this
    project, please open an issue and the maintainers will act on it.

    https://github.com/dengopaiv/ihamaics/issues
